WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.190
But this is something
you can reason about.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.403
Whereas P does not
equal NP, we don't yet

00:00:05.403 --> 00:00:06.570
know how to reason about it.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.590
People have been working
on it for 35 years--

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:17.700
it still seems difficult.
So that is complexity.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.950
Any questions about this?

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.745
So we're still deciding
exactly-- when you take 6.046,

00:00:23.745 --> 00:00:24.870
which I hope you all will--

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:25.807
[CELLPHONE RINGING]
--next semester.

00:00:25.807 --> 00:00:26.630
Oh, sorry.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.860
Jeez, it's embarrassing
to get a phone

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.160
call in the middle of class.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:30.660
Hello?

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.610
[LAUGHING]

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:36.050
Oh, it's-- oh, it's my
collaborators who have been

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.110
working on this P versus
NP problem [INAUDIBLE]..

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.120
Seriously?

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.240
P equals NP?

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.120
Holy shit.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.755
You see, what this means--

00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:48.110
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:51.960
I mean, all these problems
we thought were hard

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:52.830
are suddenly easy.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:56.430
Cryptography that you use
on the internet and the web,

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:57.388
oh, my god.

00:00:57.388 --> 00:00:59.180
You guys are the first
to learn about this.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.040
I'll call you back.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:02.400
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.434
This is, uh, when...

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:19.860
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:23.420
Professor Demaine
has been unstable recently

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.310
and he has been saying
a lot of nonsense.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:26.870
He's very sick.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:27.840
He needs to recover.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:31.110
He will not join you
for next lecture.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:38.060
Please join us to wish him
a prompt and full recovery.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.510
[APPLAUSE]

